[32m+[m[32m<p>Lots of my viewing seems to be done on YouTube these days. I like that some weekend mornings I can wake up and watch J-League football from Japan. I also like that television shows such as the Mock the Week reboot are released online and on their new TV channel — I am more likely to watch it on YouTube because of fewer clicks, I think. I went from watching British basketball all the time when they broadcast exclusively on YouTube to hardly ever since they started primarily broadcasting on DAZN. Some of the bigger basketball matches do get broadcast on YouTube; however, Caledonia Gladiators barely get a look in. I am happy to watch a podcast these days like Rest Is Entertainment or Pablo Torre Finds Out — there is no real difference between watching or listening other than one has visuals. It's not like Torre is juggling fruit. I think it's just a weird preference thing that I will watch some but only listen to others when their content is just sitting and talking.</p>[m[41m [m
